# #947: this line was "test" -- a directory that does not exist. Docker ignore
# patterns are filepath.Match against the context-relative path, anchored at the
# context root, and "*" does not cross "/", so "test" matched the literal path
# "test" and nothing else. Meanwhile api/backend/tests is 6.6M -- larger than
# src/ (4.6M) and ~55% of the production image's application payload.
#
# It cannot simply become "tests": .dockerignore is per-CONTEXT, not per
# Dockerfile, and compose.prod.yml (Dockerfile.prod) and compose.test.yml
# (Dockerfile.dev) share context ./api/backend. compose.test.yml's
# backend-unit-runner mounts only ./frontend and ./docs -- there is no
# ./api/backend:/app bind-mount -- so it runs current-state:ci
# (package.json:50) from the IMAGE LAYER, and that needs tests/architecture and
# tests/compliance. It is the only "Run backend test suite" step in CI
# (ci-pipeline.yml:176-181).
#
# So exclude only what NO container needs. Verified: no compose service and no
# CI step runs backend vitest, and tests/architecture + tests/compliance require
# nothing outside ../../src. compose.dev.yml:51 bind-mounts the real tree over
# /app, so dev is unaffected either way. This is 6.2M of the 6.6M.
tests/unit
tests/integration
*.md
.git
.gitignore

# #947: runtime data roots. Dockerfile.prod's COPY . . otherwise bakes whatever a developer's local stack has written into the production image -- including api/backend/storage/samples/**, which held a tracked personal PDF (untracked by #961, still in a local checkout). Nothing in any image needs these: prod mounts named volumes at /data/{uploads,storage,backups} per 092c4f52, and compose.test.yml mounts uploads-test-data at /app/uploads.
uploads
storage
backups
